    id: "14f5fcd4e7a8ff87b02d",
    cat: "geopolitica",
    title: "Russian strikes kill Ukrainian woman as NATO jet downs drone over Romania",
    summary: "Romania's Defence Ministry didn't specify origin of the drone but has previously blamed Russia for similar incidents.",
    preview: "Ukraine targets Moscow in mass drone attack as Russia bombards Kyiv Romania’s Defence Ministry didn’t specify the origin of the drone but has previously blamed Russia for similar incidents. At least one person has been killed in and three others were wounded in a Ukrainian drone barrage targeting Moscow, a local official said, as Russia bombarded Kyiv with ballistic missiles.",
    body: "Ukraine targets Moscow in mass drone attack as Russia bombards Kyiv\n\nRomania’s Defence Ministry didn’t specify the origin of the drone but has previously blamed Russia for similar incidents.\n\nAt least one person has been killed in and three others were wounded in a Ukrainian drone barrage targeting Moscow, a local official said, as Russia bombarded Kyiv with ballistic missiles.\n\nMoscow Mayor Sergei Sobyanin wrote on social media early Sunday that the city had been targeted with 600 drones and that “201 drones were destroyed in Moscow region.”\n\nRecommended Stories\n\nlist of 3 items\n\n- list 1 of 3Russia says hit Ukrainian railway and port facilities in new strikes\n\n- list 2 of 3Russia stance will be defended in court, pledges World Athletics chief Coe\n\n- list 3 of 3Ukraine hits Russian Starlink-style network, Moscow tracks arms package\n\nAndrei Vorobyov, Governor of Moscow Oblast, wrote on Telegram that an 83-year-old man was killed after a drone hit a private home.\n\nAt least three other people were killed in attacks on Russia’s southern Rostov region, which borders Ukraine, according to regional authorities.\n\nThe drone assault comes after Ukrainian authorities said at least one person was killed and seven others were wounded in Russian air attacks.\n\nA woman was killed and six others were wounded in a missile and drone attack on Kryvyi Rig, the hometown of President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in central Ukraine, the region’s governor said.\n\nOfficials in the capital said Kyiv was “under ballistic missile attack” late on Saturday, with at least one person wounded and fires sparked at non-residential sites in the Obolonsky and Holosiivskyi districts.\n\nSeparately, Romania’s Defence Ministry reported on Sunday that a Spanish F-18 fighter jet pilot on a NATO air policing mission to Romania had shot down a drone illegally breaching its national airspace.\n\nIt is the fourth drone shot down in Romania this year.\n\nRomania’s Defence Ministry wrote on social media that the drone came from neighbouring country Moldova.\n\n“The surveillance systems of the Ministry of National Defense detected the intrusion of an aerial target into national airspace, coming from the Republic of Moldova,” it said in a statement.\n\nDefence Minister Radu Miruta congratulated the pilots and military personnel on what he called “a successful mission.”\n\nIn July, a Romanian jet shot down a suspected Russian drone, and in May a stray drone injured two people in the Romanian city of Galati when it collided with a building.\n\nRomania shares a 634km (394-mile) border with Ukraine and has repeatedly seen Russian drones breaching its airspace as Moscow escalates its bombing campaign against Ukrainian civilian and military infrastructure.\n\nEscalating long-range strikes\n\nRussia has maintained near-daily missile and drone strikes across Ukraine since launching its full-scale invasion in early 2022, with areas far from the front lines frequently coming under attack.\n\nThe war’s impact has also spread to key regional shipping lanes, with reports of mines and unmanned sea drones found floating in the Black Sea.\n\nCivilian casualties in Ukraine hit their highest level since 2022 this July, with at least 437 killed and 2,610 injured, according to the United Nations Human Rights Monitoring Mission.\n\nUkraine has increasingly targeted military, industrial and logistical facilities deep inside Russia, arguing its strikes are a response to Moscow’s ongoing bombardment of Ukrainian towns and infrastructure.",
